        "body": "Hi Emma, we've looked over Arc. The chain is worn out and the gear cluster on the back wheel (the cassette) is worn too. That's why the gears skip when you pedal hard in the smaller gears. A new chain on its own wouldn't fix it, because it would still slip on the worn gears. So we'd fit a new chain and a new cassette. We'd use the same 11-34 range as you have now, and it works with your carbon wheels. The total is $169.98, which covers both parts and the labor. The new cassette has to be ordered in, so Arc will be ready on Saturday, November 21. You can approve or decline the quote below.",
